🚀 Step-by-Step Guide & README
This guide covers everything from zero installation to running your live AI + AR Smart Object Recognition System on your smartphone.

📋 Prerequisites
Before starting, make sure you have:

PHP 8.3 or higher with the curl extension enabled.

A local web server such as XAMPP, WAMP, Laragon, or a live hosting server (cPanel / VPS).

A Google AI Studio API Key (Free).

🛠️ Step 1: Download & Folder Setup
Copy the project files into your web server root directory:

For XAMPP (Windows): C:\xampp\htdocs\ai-ar-object-recognition\

For cPanel Hosting: public_html/ai-ar/

Ensure your directory structure matches the following layout:

Plaintext
ai-ar-object-recognition/
├── index.php
├── settings.php
├── README.md
├── api/
│   ├── recognize.php
│   └── settings.php
├── config/
│   ├── config.example.php
│   └── config.php
├── includes/
│   ├── AppConfig.php
│   ├── AIProvider.php
│   ├── GeminiVision.php
│   ├── AgnesVision.php
│   └── ImageValidator.php
└── assets/
    ├── css/
    │   └── app.css
    └── js/
        ├── camera.js
        ├── voice.js
        ├── haptic.js
        ├── ar-overlay.js
        ├── scanner.js
        └── settings.js
🔑 Step 2: Get Your Free Gemini API Key
Go to Google AI Studio.

Log in with your Google account.

Click on "Get API key" and select "Create API key".

Copy your new API key string.

⚙️ Step 3: System Configuration
Open your browser and navigate to the settings page:

Local: http://localhost/ai-ar-object-recognition/settings.php

Scroll to the AI Provider & API Keys section.

Paste your key into the Gemini API Key input field.

Set the Gemini Model to:

Plaintext
gemini-3.8-flash
In the Voice Narration Settings section:

Choose your preferred country voice accent (e.g., 🇲🇾 Malaysia, 🇯🇵 Japan, 🇺🇸 US, 🇬🇧 UK).

Adjust the volume slider and click Test Voice to verify audio output.

Click Save All Settings.

📱 Step 4: Connecting via Smartphone (HTTPS Requirement)
⚠️ Important: Modern smartphone web browsers require a secure connection (HTTPS) to allow web pages to access camera hardware (navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia).

Option A: Hosting on Live Server (Recommended)
Upload your files to your HTTPS-enabled domain or cPanel hosting.

Open [https://your-domain.com/ai-ar/settings.php](https://your-domain.com/ai-ar/settings.php).

Scroll down to the Open Scanner on Smartphone section to reveal the automatically generated QR code.
![App Preview](assets/images/scanner-preview.png)
Scan the QR code using your phone's default camera app to open the live scanner!

Option B: Testing Locally on Same Wi-Fi (Using Ngrok for HTTPS)
If running XAMPP on your computer:

Download and run Ngrok.

Expose your local server port by running:

Bash
ngrok http 80
Copy the secure HTTPS URL provided by Ngrok (e.g., [https://xxxx.ngrok-free.app/ai-ar-object-recognition/](https://xxxx.ngrok-free.app/ai-ar-object-recognition/)) and open it on your phone.

📸 Step 5: Using the AR Scanner
![App Preview](assets/images/image-1.png)
Camera Permission: When prompted on your phone, tap Allow to grant camera permission.

Focus: Tap anywhere on the live camera preview to trigger Tap-to-Focus with the animated reticle.

Flashlight: Tap the Flashlight icon (⚡) in the top menu to toggle torch light in dark areas.

Switch Camera: Tap the Camera Switch icon (🔄) to cycle between back, front, and wide lenses.
![App Preview](assets/images/image-2.png)
Scan Object: Point your camera at an object and press the large blue Scan Button.

Results & AR Overlay:

The system captures and compresses the image frame.

AI identifies the object and draws an AR Bounding Box over it.

The Product Card pops up displaying the product name, specs, and description.

The system automatically reads aloud the result in your selected voice!